CTCP replies, from mIRC's Ctcp Events help section. /halt stops the
client's own reply.

-- ctcp.mrc --
ctcp *:PING:?:notice $nick Ouch! | halt
ctcp *:TIME:*:notice $nick The time here is around $time
ctcp 5:OPME:?:mode $2 +o $nick
ctcp *:SLAP:?:{
  if ($2) describe $nick slaps $2 back
  halt
}
-- transcript --
! ctcp.mrc: line 3: level 5 needs the Users list, which trout doesn't have; this event never triggers
me trout
clock 2026-10-29T15:04:05Z
< :bob!b@host PRIVMSG trout :\x01PING 12345\x01
> /notice bob Ouch!
* halted
# A channel CTCP: PING is only for private ones (?).
< :bob!b@host PRIVMSG #trout :\x01PING 12345\x01
< :bob!b@host PRIVMSG #trout :\x01TIME\x01
> /notice bob The time here is around 15:04:05
< :bob!b@host PRIVMSG trout :\x01OPME #trout\x01
< :bob!b@host PRIVMSG trout :\x01SLAP alice\x01
> /describe bob slaps alice back
* halted
< :bob!b@host PRIVMSG trout :\x01SLAP\x01
* halted
# Our own CTCPs aren't events.
< :trout!t@host PRIVMSG bob :\x01PING 1\x01
# An action isn't a CTCP event.
< :bob!b@host PRIVMSG trout :\x01ACTION pings\x01
